# dev

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Query outputs — never commit the results of running the SQL to this repo.
# The MLRS and NLSDB extracts are PUBLIC data: BLM provides no PII or sensitive
# data, so the SQL and its comments may name cases, serials and values freely.
# This repo holds code and documentation only; outputs (CSV/XLSX results,
# client spreadsheets) go to the sibling folder
# D:\Xentity\BLM\BLM_DQIMP_GitRepo\Query_Results\ (outside this tree). These
# rules are a second layer of protection in case an output is ever written to
# the repo folder.
# NOTE: existing tracked files (e.g. web-app/*.csv, the lookup-table CSV under
# schemas/) are unaffected — .gitignore does not untrack committed files.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
*_results.csv
*_results_*.csv
*__part*.csv
*.xlsx
*.xls
/Query_Results/
query_results/
*.results.csv
*.load
*.parquet
*.zip
*.tar
*.gz
*.gdb/
Full_Load_Log_*.txt
prepare_snapshot_log_*.txt
BigQuery_Load_log_*.txt
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.venv/
.ipynb_checkpoints/
.vscode/settings.json
# Monthly build: machine-specific paths and Claude Code personal settings
build/monthly_build.local.json
.claude/settings.local.json
# Dashboard update agent (web-app/): per-machine pins, personal Claude Code settings, and
# outputs if the flat BLM layout is ever reproduced inside the repo
web-app/tests/guard_pins.json
web-app/.claude/settings.local.json
web-app/Query_Results/
# Build agent (build/ is its home): personal Claude Code settings and VS Code settings there
build/.claude/settings.local.json
build/.vscode/settings.json
